## Cursor auto-generates

When Cursor auto-generates a Git commit message for this repository, I would like you to use English and commit message less than 100 characters.

## Code style

- **Early return:** Prefer guard clauses at the top of a function (`if (!precondition) return;` or `return false;`). Handle invalid state first so the “happy path” stays flat and readable at the bottom.
- **`if` bodies:** Use `{ }` whenever the body has more than one statement. If the body is **only** a `return` (including `return value;`), it may be written on one line: `if (cond) return value;`
- **Loops:** Prefer `while (true)` over `for (;;)` for infinite loops. Use `{ }` whenever the loop body has more than one statement. A single-statement body may stay on one line if it stays clear (e.g. `if (!f) break;`).
- **Long `&&` chains:** If one expression uses **more than three** operands joined by `&&` (i.e. **three or more** `&&` operators), break it across lines: keep the first operand on the first line, then put each `&& …` at the **beginning** of the next line, aligned with the same indent as the opening `if`/`while`/`return` (continuation lines indented one level if that reads better).
- **Spacing:** Always leave exactly one blank line between function definitions (including member functions defined in headers).

## Naming conventions

- **snake_case:** Use `snake_case` for functions and variables.
- **No trailing underscore:** Do not use the `_` suffix for variable names (e.g. avoid `foo_`).

## Module structure (ESP32/LVGL project)

- **Header-only modules:** Each module is a `Class` whose full implementation lives in its `*.h` file.
- **`*.cpp` instantiation only:** Each module `*.cpp` contains only `#include "<module>.h"` and the single global instance definition.
- **Interface:** Modules implement the common interface in `src/modules/common/imodule.h` (`setup()`, `loop_ui()`, `loop()`), typically via `ModuleOnce` so `setup()` is idempotent (setup-once behavior).
- **Public surface:** Keep only necessary APIs `public`; prefer `private`/`protected` for the rest.
- **Callbacks/tasks:** Use the macros in `src/modules/common/helpers.h`:
    - `LV_OBJ_EVENT_CB(Class, method)` for LVGL event callbacks
    - `FREERTOS_TASK_CB(Class, method)` for FreeRTOS task entry points
      Avoid adding `static` trampoline methods inside classes.
- **Comments:** Do not remove existing author comments. If a comment must be moved/edited for refactors, preserve its content.

## Project hardware reference (`README.md`)

- **Read** [`README.md`](README.md) when work touches this board (ESP32-S3 **ES3C28P** / **ES3N28P**, 2.8" ILI9341, touch, SD, audio, pins): pinout, buses (SPI MOSI/MISO, I2C, SDIO, I2S), and wiki links live there.
